# What Results to Expect from the Kiro Implementation

This is a critical question, because **what you expect shapes what you will accept as correct.** If you expect positive results and get a null, you may misinterpret the null as failure. If you expect a null and get a positive, you may misinterpret the positive as fabricated. Below is a **calibrated expectation** for each stage of the execution, based on what the design can plausibly produce and what the search results, the DGP structure, and the estimator characteristics imply.

